text.paragraph:
In pediatric trials of dasatinib in chronic phase CML after at least 2 years of treatment, adverse reactions associated with bone growth and development were reported in 5 (5.2%) patients, one of which was severe in intensity (Growth Retardation Grade 3). These 5 cases included cases of epiphyses delayed fusion, osteopenia, growth retardation, and gynecomastia [see Adverse Reactions (6.1) and Use in Specific Populations (8.4
                              )]
                           . Of these 5 cases, 1 case of osteopenia and 1 case of gynecomastia resolved during treatment.
